A hosted screen draws its conversation before its extensions bind.

pi's startup binds every extension, awaiting each one's session_start in
turn, and only then draws the conversation. On a busy machine a host's
opens spent 48 to 146 s in that bind, most of it in four extensions'
session_start handlers reading shared state off a stalled disk, and the
person's window stayed blank the whole time: nothing on it said which
conversation it was or what had been said.

A hosted screen now draws the conversation's messages first and sends
that frame at once, since a session_start holding the thread would hold
a frame only requested. That helps a viewer already attached; one who
joins while a session_start holds the thread is drawn once it lets go,
as before. It then binds, and after the bind draws only the entries the
extensions' session_start added meanwhile, where startup would have
drawn them all. Nothing already on the screen is cleared, so the
notices startup made before the bind stay. Where the bind did more than
add (a compaction, a move in the tree, a shorter branch), so the entries
drawn are no longer the conversation's first, the chat is built again
from the conversation as it now is, which drops those notices and any
error the bind showed, rather than show a conversation the agent no
longer holds. It is built again too where the early draw left a tool
call waiting on its result and the bind added entries, since pi matches
a result to its call only within one draw. The resources pi lists once
its extensions bind still land above the conversation, in their own
container. Tool and message renderers are registered as extensions load,
before the bind, so the early draw has them; one that reads state its
session_start loads draws those messages without it, and they stay so
drawn until the chat is next built. One that throws for want of that
state takes back only what the early draw added, so the notices before
it stay and no prompt lands in the editor's history twice, and the
conversation is drawn after the bind, as startup draws it. It hears the
agent only once the bind ends, as before, so nothing reaches an
extension before its hooks are live. A plain pi starts as before.

Apply only to the host's private pi build; ordinary interactive pi stays
unchanged.

